WEBVTT

00:17:58.596 --> 00:18:00.796
S: The cognitive dissonance just grows.

00:18:00.836 --> 00:18:02.156
DP: Yes, exactly.

00:18:02.196 --> 00:18:04.996
Well, thank you for sharing your story.

00:18:04.996 --> 00:18:06.716
WPR: As you're doing this work,

00:18:06.756 --> 00:18:09.396
having these conversations
and writing this book,

00:18:09.436 --> 00:18:10.676
what have you --

00:18:10.716 --> 00:18:12.956
how are you feeling,
I guess, about the future?

00:18:12.956 --> 00:18:16.396
DP: I want to be really clear about that
because it is a very heavy book.

00:18:16.436 --> 00:18:19.556
There is a lot that's there
that can make you really feel sad.

00:18:19.596 --> 00:18:20.916
But the overall message,

00:18:20.956 --> 00:18:23.236
and there is a tone to it
that is very powerful,

00:18:23.236 --> 00:18:24.556
like, I'm very optimistic.

00:18:24.556 --> 00:18:29.756
I met amazing women with amazing skills
who I think have different visions

00:18:29.796 --> 00:18:32.156
for what our future looks like.